  "bug_info": "Summary of configuration for Project: Collections\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Script dir: /root/defects4j/framework\n      Base dir: /root/defects4j\n    Major root: /root/defects4j/major\n      Repo dir: /root/defects4j/project_repos\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Project ID: Collections\n       Program: commons-collections\n    Build file: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Collections/Collections.build.xml\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n           Vcs: Vcs::Git\n    Repository: /root/defects4j/project_repos/commons-collections.git\n     Commit db: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Collections/active-bugs.csv\nNumber of bugs: 28\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSummary for Bug: Collections-15\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision ID (fixed version):\n0122245f02ba7b22dd40f38c98aa2f08984707bd\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision date (fixed version):\n2008-11-05 15:47:43 +0000\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report id:\nCOLLECTIONS-304\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report url:\nhttps://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/COLLECTIONS-304\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRoot cause in triggering tests:\n - org.apache.commons.collections.list.TestSetUniqueList::testCollections304\n   --> junit.framework.AssertionFailedError: expected:<3> but was:<4>\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nList of modified sources:\n - org.apache.commons.collections.list.SetUniqueList\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------",
  "bug_report_content": "Title: SetUniqueList set method use corrupts uniqness\nType: Bug | Priority: Major | Status: Closed | Resolution: Fixed\n\nDescription:\nWhen set method is used to put element (Strawberry) on list, then it is possible to add the same element (Strawberry) with add method. Also you cannot add element (Lemon) that has been once removed with set method. Reproduction code below:\n\n\nList<String> list = new LinkedList<String>();\nSetUniqueList decoratedList = SetUniqueList.decorate(list);\n\ndecoratedList.add(\"Apple\");\ndecoratedList.add(\"Lemon\");\ndecoratedList.add(\"Orange\");\n\nSystem.out.println(decoratedList.toString());\n\ndecoratedList.set(1, \"Strawberry\");\n\nSystem.out.println(decoratedList.toString());\n\ndecoratedList.add(1, \"Strawberry\");\n\nSystem.out.println(decoratedList.toString());\n\ndecoratedList.add(1, \"Lemon\");\n\nSystem.out.println(decoratedList.toString());\n\nComments:\n\n[Bjorn Townsend]: Here's a JUnit test reproducing this. Nice catch. :)\n\n[Henri Yandell]: Adding a fix for this issue, with a slight tweak on Bjorn's unit test.\n\n[Henri Yandell]: svn ci -m \"Applying Bjorn Townsend's unit test and my fix for COLLECTIONS-304 - fixing SetUniqueList so the set method doesn't let the uniqueness get out of sync\"\nSending        src/java/org/apache/commons/collections/list/SetUniqueList.java\nSending        src/test/org/apache/commons/collections/list/TestSetUniqueList.java\nTransmitting file data ..\nCommitted revision 711591.",
  "fix_diff": "--- org.apache.commons.collections.list.SetUniqueList (buggy)\n+++ org.apache.commons.collections.list.SetUniqueList (fixed)\n@@ -221,13 +221,13 @@\n         int pos = indexOf(object);\n         Object removed = super.set(index, object);\n \n-        if (pos == -1 || pos == index) {\n+        if (pos != -1 && pos != index) {\n             // the object is already in the uniq list\n             // (and it hasn't been swapped with itself)\n-            return removed;\n-        }\n-\n-        super.remove(pos);\n+            super.remove(pos);  // remove the duplicate by index\n+        }\n+\n+        set.add(object);      // add the new item to the unique set\n         set.remove(removed);  // remove the item deleted by the set\n \n         return removed;  // return the item deleted by the set"
}